# Cursor rules

- One topic per file: `.cursor/rules/<kebab-case>.mdc` with frontmatter `description`, `globs`, `alwaysApply`.
- Prefer glob-scoped rules with `alwaysApply: false`. Keep always-on rules short; repo-wide conventions belong in the repo's `AGENTS.md`.
- Do not repeat `AGENTS.md` or another rule; link to it.
- Personal preferences stay out of repos; they live in dotfiles.
- Keep `.cursor/rules/README.md` as the index when a repo has one.
